// The demo orders (issue #187): the orders collection and its lines,
// generated by Payload, and the pickup point's price in "Shop settings",
// 3.90 € by default (owner decision, 2026-11-17). Then, hand-written:
// - order_numbers, the sequence an order's number comes from when it is
//   placed, so drafts use none and two orders never share one;
// - a trigger capping the table at MAX_ORDERS rows, drafts included
//   (site/checkout-rules.ts), so the stored data stays within Neon's free
//   plan, as customers_cap does for accounts: each insert waits for the lock
//   until the other's transaction ends, then counts.
// tests/orders-db.test.ts checks the cap matches MAX_ORDERS.
